@@ -1,6 +1,15 @@
 # Changelog
 
 Dated, factual, one line per change. Newest first.
+
+## 2026-11-12 - Phase 4, Block E3 (agent model harmonised with the morale model, twin fix, Table 40 revisions, sign-off sheet)
+- E3.1: the agent and tier simulations use the tax-morale model's mechanism: interventions (USSD TIN nudge for mobile-money users, civic tax education for urban adults 18+) multiply each agent's yearly registration ODDS by the model's odds ratios (1.243, 1.304; 1.336 for agents reached by both, by the model's combination rule: driver deltas summed after x `tax_morale.combined_discount`). The trust / morale uplift path and the community-norm feedback are retired: 7 constants (agents.ussd.*, agents.edu.morale_uplift_*, agents.norm_uplift_factor) RETIRED, reason 'replaced by morale-model odds ratios (E3.1)'. The no-intervention path changed, so the E2.4 calibration was re-run (same target and method): conversion 0.0069, intercept -0.251, RMSE 0.228 pp, correlation -0.99; identified combination conversion x (mean index + intercept) = 0.332% a year. Year-10 registration 7.67% with the interventions vs 6.98% without (effect 0.69 pp; was +0.30 pp); tier year 10: 92.3 / 0.2 / 0.9 / 2.0 / 1.8 / 2.8%. C062 is still BLOCKED by the four agents.p_comply weights.
+- E3.2: third calibration target searched (FinScope 2017 published TIN rate, TRA / NBS individual-entity split, yearly new registrations): none compatible and available (the 2017 questionnaire asks the TIN document item but the 2017 report prints no TIN rate); the two-target calibration is kept and its identified combination reported (`agent_calibration.json` identifiability.identified_combination, third_target_search).
+- E3.3: digital twin: `base.mobile_money_users` = FinScope 2023 weighted adult mobile-money users (24.4 million, DATA); BoT's 63.2 million accounts are a context figure only; new `base.adult_population` (FinScope weighted adults, DATA) and `twin.growth.adult_population` (WDI); mobile-money penetration rises toward `twin.mm.penetration_cap` (0.90, ASSUMPTION, not signed) closing `twin.mm.penetration_gap_closure` (0.10) of the gap each year; the USSD term applies only to unregistered users; registrations and users can never exceed adults (asserted). `twin.growth.mm_users` and `twin.cap.mm_users_share_of_population` RETIRED. Policy scenario year 10: tax-to-GDP 16.69% (was 17.40%), registrations 29,938,239.0 (was 34.0 million) against 45,503,951 adults. Outputs labelled 'MODELLED scenario'.
+- E3.4: Table 40: stage mechanisms carry the report's own names (Targeting Priority Tool, Mzani wa Kodi, Ngazi Progression Dashboard, Mali Alama, Kodi Legacy Score and Succession Builder; Seed Madarasa Ya Kodi); 10-year results unchanged; 20-year sensitivity with the cohort's ILFS age-earnings path (ROI medians entry 0.67x, active 11.75x, enterprise 4.91x, legacy 0.27x) and at persistence 0.75 / 0.90 / 0.95; Asset: 617.5M placeholder RETIRED, break-even cost reported (below TZS 2.08 billion); Asset excluded from the portfolio (without Asset: ROI median 3.67x, NPV median TZS 8.50 billion). New columns in `table40_stage_economics.csv`, new blocks in `stage_economics.json`.
+- E3.5: sign-offs recorded (approved, John, 2026-11-12): the five tier.* filing constants, tax_morale.baseline.enforcement, stage.reach_share, stage.intervention_for_uptake, stage.uptake_log_odds_sd, stage.persistence, stage.ramp_years, stage.horizon_years, stage.discount_rate, stage.discount_sensitivities, stage.cost_overrun_sigma, stage.cost.* (not Asset). A signed-off UNKNOWN constant no longer blocks its claims. The twin penetration cap is NOT signed.
+- E3.6: `docs/signoff_sheet.csv` and `docs/signoff_sheet.md` (new `src/tools/build_signoff_sheet.py`): every unsigned ASSUMPTION / UNKNOWN row by area with sensitivity and a recommendation; `assumption_sensitivity.py` gained the Table 40 runner and the design rows.
+- Tests: `test_agent_odds_ratios.py`, `test_digital_twin.py` (new); `test_stage_economics.py`, `test_agent_calibration.py`, `test_assumptions.py`, `test_tra_series.py` updated.
 
 ## 2026-11-12 - Phase 4, Block E2 (data sourcing, model recalibration, W11 Table 40)
 - E2.0 decisions recorded: the PRIMARY targeting model is the refit without the REQUIRES_TIN feature (business vehicle; AUC 0.946, Entry multiplier 6.55x, interval 5.80-7.14x); the all-features model and the fit without UNCERTAIN items are comparison / sensitivity fits (`targeting_model.json variants`, `outputs/tables/targeting_variants.csv`). `tax_morale.baseline.simplicity` is DATA (Afrobarometer Q46A, reversed, 'information burden only'); `agents.non_earners_zero_income` carries `signoff: approved (John, 2026-11-12)` (register column `john_signoff`); the simulations carry a `status` ('UN-RECALIBRATED - NOT FOR PUBLICATION' until the E2.4 calibration succeeds).
