+## Closed in Block E3 (2026-11-12)
+- Agent and tier simulations use the same mechanism as the morale model (odds ratios on the yearly registration odds); the trust / morale uplift path and its 7 constants are retired.
+- Digital twin: users and registrations can never exceed adults; the user base is FinScope adult users (persons), not BoT accounts; the USSD term applies to unregistered users only; outputs are labelled MODELLED scenario.
+- Table 40: Asset placeholder cost removed (break-even cost reported); portfolio computed without Asset; 20-year sensitivity with an age-earnings path and a persistence sensitivity.
+- Sign-offs recorded; a signed-off UNKNOWN constant no longer blocks its claims; sign-off sheet written (`docs/signoff_sheet.md`).
 
 ## Closed in Block E2 (2026-11-12)
